From 0d61372d948ebf3a6e48ea1396c99217905135e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ayush Gupta <ag789439@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:51:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Marks sheet never dead-ends; public landing page for search

- a subject that is not on the exam schedule no longer stops the screen: the
  grid loads with max 100 / pass 33 and says so
- the roster falls back from an exact class match to a loose one, then to all
  active students, instead of showing an empty grid
- a clear empty state when there is genuinely nobody to list
- '/' now serves a public landing page to signed-out visitors, so a search
  engine has something to read; signed-in users still get the dashboard
- sitemap lists the landing page and the login page
---
 app.py | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app.py b/app.py
index 1d55958..d80405d 100644
--- a/app.py
+++ b/app.py
@@ -80,9 +80,11 @@ TEMPLATES = {
     'schedule.html':
